From a4917a06f7ddaec08dd7e18f854149e48531f145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 04:08:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Supabase backend: auth, cloud sync, and live facilitator
 dashboard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New tables (prefixed mapan_ to avoid collision with existing Supabase project): mapan_profiles, mapan_journey_state (full state blob per user), mapan_checkin_results (denormalized, for live dashboard)
- RLS enabled on all 3 tables: users can only read/write their own rows; checkin_results is readable by any signed-in user (for the dashboard)
- Realtime enabled on mapan_checkin_results
- New Login.jsx screen (signup/signin), wired in after Welcome's 'Mulai Perjalanan'
- store.js: tracks Supabase auth session, pulls saved journey_state on login, pushes state to Supabase (debounced) on every update, exposes signUp/signIn/signOut/syncCheckinResult
- CheckIn.jsx: pushes check-in scores to mapan_checkin_results on completion
- New Dashboard.jsx: live facilitator view via Supabase Realtime — per-domain averages + recent submissions feed, accessible from Profil
- Profil.jsx: privacy copy updated to reflect cloud storage (no longer claims device-only), added Sign Out button and Dashboard link
- Supabase URL + anon/publishable key added via .env (safe to expose client-side; protection comes from RLS, not secrecy)

NOTE: could not fully browser-test signup/login end-to-end — this sandbox's network egress does not allow reaching *.supabase.co (confirmed via direct curl: 'Host not in allowlist'). Database schema, RLS, and Realtime were verified directly via the Supabase API/SQL, which is unaffected by this restriction. Please test the live signup flow once deployed.
